<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>It is to those that fear His name</l><l>His healing power the Savior brings;</l><l>Oh, let us hide with contrite hearts</l><l>Beneath His healing wings.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>He is the Sun of Righteousness;</l><l>And while to sin our being clings</l><l>We cannot know His healing touch</l><l>Or rest beneath His wings.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>It is His wings that heal our pains</l><l>And soothe the serpent’s poisoned stings;</l><l>Close to His bosom we must press</l><l>To feel His healing wings.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>Beneath those healing wings I rest,</l><l>While all my heart with rapture sings:</l><l>The Sun of Righteousness has risen</l><l>With healing in His wings.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
